He argued that the Investigating Agency before the registration of FIR had registered a Preliminary Verification, during which the Investigating agency admittedly in the FIR have examined the following aspects:
 a) Various communications of NRHM;
 b) Communications of Directorate of Health Services Srinagar  as well as Jammu;
 c) Guidelines issued by Ministry of Health and Family Welfare,
 Government of India;
 d) Rates on which Drug Kits were purchased during the year  2009-2010;
 e) The corrigendum issued by Director Health Services,
 Kashmir;
 f) The alleged fact that the supplies were allegedly made by private agencies from Indore and not by CPSEs.
